13
00:02:47.793 --> 00:02:51.338
- A lot of historical interest
in this place.

14
00:02:51.380 --> 00:02:53.882
The older section
of the house was built

15
00:02:53.924 --> 00:02:58.011
in Victoria's coronation year.

16
00:02:58.053 --> 00:02:59.763
The plan was a month.

17
00:02:59.805 --> 00:03:02.891
but the parish lines
were redrawn.

18
00:03:02.933 --> 00:03:04.643
The next person to live here
was the son

19
00:03:04.685 --> 00:03:06.562
of one of the local lairds.

20
00:03:06.603 --> 00:03:10.566
- Oh. When was the roof
last replaced?

21
00:03:10.607 --> 00:03:12.526
- Must have been '70.

22
00:03:12.568 --> 00:03:17.114
Well. but it's hard slate.
so should last for 100 years.

23
00:03:17.155 --> 00:03:19.658
Come. In you go
and have a look round.

24
00:03:43.098 --> 00:03:46.310
[ominous music]

25
00:03:46.351 --> 00:03:50.147
[dark piano notes]

26
00:03:55.777 --> 00:03:58.238
- Imagine it without this room.

27
00:03:58.280 --> 00:04:02.534
- Who ever thought
this was a good idea?

28
00:04:02.576 --> 00:04:04.828
- Well. do you think
the fireplaces still work?

29
00:04:04.870 --> 00:04:06.413
- [speaking indistinctly]

30
00:04:10.209 --> 00:04:12.377
- I can't see up this chimney.

31
00:04:16.340 --> 00:04:17.883
Either it's been blocked.

32
00:04:17.925 --> 00:04:20.802
or there's a bird's nest
in there.

33
00:04:22.721 --> 00:04:24.431
- I think it's blocked.

34
00:04:24.473 --> 00:04:27.059
- [speaking indistinctly]

35
00:04:29.394 --> 00:04:35.400
[ominous music continues]

36
00:04:44.034 --> 00:04:48.247
[indistinct chatter]

37
