144
00:24:32.431 --> 00:24:34.183
[sighs]

145
00:24:36.268 --> 00:24:37.936
[door clicks shut]

146
00:25:02.878 --> 00:25:05.839
[footsteps tapping]

147
00:25:15.557 --> 00:25:18.560
[birds singing]

148
00:26:04.147 --> 00:26:07.150
[car engine rumbling]

149
00:26:15.617 --> 00:26:18.829
[car door clicks open. slams]

150
00:26:29.423 --> 00:26:30.424
[metallic thud]

151
00:26:30.465 --> 00:26:33.468
[indistinct chatter]

152
00:26:36.430 --> 00:26:38.849
[lock clicking]

153
00:26:41.143 --> 00:26:42.686
[door creaks]

154
00:26:42.728 --> 00:26:44.479
- Thanks for making
the time for this.

155
00:26:44.521 --> 00:26:46.273
- Not at all.

156
00:26:46.315 --> 00:26:49.526
So as you can see.

157
00:26:49.568 --> 00:26:52.529
there's a real wealth
of history.

158
00:26:52.571 --> 00:26:54.364
Not many like these anymore.

159
00:26:54.406 --> 00:26:55.824
- Mm.

160
00:26:57.284 --> 00:26:59.912
- Oh. the electricity's
been turned off

161
00:26:59.953 --> 00:27:01.663
to be friendly
to the environment.

162
00:27:01.705 --> 00:27:03.874
- Henry. get your phone out.

163
00:27:03.916 --> 00:27:06.001
- The first part of this house
was built

164
00:27:06.043 --> 00:27:10.255
at the very beginning
of the Victorian age.

165
00:27:10.297 --> 00:27:13.300
[indistinct chatter]

166
00:27:16.720 --> 00:27:19.723
[indistinct chatter]

167
00:27:23.227 --> 00:27:26.230
[static crackling]

168
00:27:26.271 --> 00:27:29.608
[ominous music]

169
00:27:35.447 --> 00:27:38.784
Did you tell anybody that you
were coming here today?

170
00:27:41.912 --> 00:27:44.206
[indistinct chatter]

171
00:27:44.248 --> 00:27:47.251
[static crackling]

172
00:27:51.463 --> 00:27:54.716
- We really just want something
more like a home. you see.

173
00:27:54.758 --> 00:27:56.552
[slapping]

174
00:27:58.637 --> 00:28:02.933
Who would want to come and stay
in a holiday let like this?

175
00:28:02.975 --> 00:28:05.978
[static crackling]

176
00:28:19.908 --> 00:28:21.910
- Might be cheaper
to tear this down

177
00:28:21.952 --> 00:28:24.329
and start with a new build.

178
00:28:25.414 --> 00:28:27.791
- Get out.

179
00:28:27.833 --> 00:28:28.959
- Henry.

180
00:28:29.001 --> 00:28:30.627
- Pardon?
- Get out.

181
00:28:30.669 --> 00:28:31.670
- Henry.

182
00:28:31.712 --> 00:28:33.130
- Get out.

183
00:28:33.172 --> 00:28:34.715
Get out!

184
00:28:36.258 --> 00:28:38.010
- Don't talk like that.

185
00:28:38.051 --> 00:28:39.636
- We don't need you here.

186
00:28:39.678 --> 00:28:42.181
- You can't talk
to us that way!

187
00:28:42.222 --> 00:28:43.390
- Get away!

188
00:28:43.432 --> 00:28:44.808
- Henry!

189
00:28:44.850 --> 00:28:47.853
[heavy breathing]

190
00:28:52.566 --> 00:28:53.650
- Go outside. Sonia.

191
00:29:01.241 --> 00:29:02.618
All right.

192
00:29:21.762 --> 00:29:23.931
You're a small man.

193
00:29:29.353 --> 00:29:31.647
- [sighs]

194
00:29:34.107 --> 00:29:35.567
[whimpers]

195
00:29:48.497 --> 00:29:51.500
[car engine rumbling]

196
00:29:55.629 --> 00:29:58.632
[footsteps tapping]

197
00:30:05.180 --> 00:30:06.849
[sighs]

198
00:30:11.103 --> 00:30:13.188
You shouldn't have this.

199
00:30:13.230 --> 00:30:14.982
I should smash it.

200
00:30:24.867 --> 00:30:27.452
What are you doing?

201
00:30:27.494 --> 00:30:29.663
You've been so hungry.
so hungry. so hungry.

202
00:30:29.705 --> 00:30:31.707
I couldn't keep up.

203
00:30:31.748 --> 00:30:33.959
Why?

204
00:30:34.001 --> 00:30:35.711
Are you full now?

205
00:30:37.421 --> 00:30:41.675
You know. they--you don't know.

206
00:30:41.717 --> 00:30:44.136
You don't understand anything.

207
00:30:44.178 --> 00:30:46.138
They'll gut you.
They'll rip you apart.

208
00:30:46.180 --> 00:30:48.265
They'll--they'll--
they'll turn you

209
00:30:48.307 --> 00:30:52.394
into something without soul.

210
00:30:52.436 --> 00:30:54.229
Something without soul.

211
00:30:54.271 --> 00:30:58.066
something--

212
00:30:58.108 --> 00:31:01.195
strangers coming to and fro.

213
00:31:04.281 --> 00:31:06.116
Or is that what you want?

214
00:31:06.158 --> 00:31:12.915
You want to rot and decay
and turn into rubble?

215
00:31:14.458 --> 00:31:18.170
Turn into a row.
a load of rubble?

216
00:31:29.348 --> 00:31:32.267
[whispering]
I won't let this happen.

217
00:32:06.468 --> 00:32:08.303
I got a letter here.

218
00:32:10.264 --> 00:32:11.765
A CPO.

219
00:32:14.852 --> 00:32:16.311
You know what that is?

220
00:32:19.314 --> 00:32:23.360
They want to take you away.

221
00:32:23.402 --> 00:32:26.363
Take you away from me.

222
00:32:26.405 --> 00:32:29.575
Own you.

223
00:32:29.616 --> 00:32:32.703
Change you.

224
00:32:32.744 --> 00:32:36.290
[sighs]

225
00:32:36.331 --> 00:32:38.292
But I'm going to sort it out.

226
00:32:40.961 --> 00:32:43.755
I'm putting
some money together.

227
00:32:43.797 --> 00:32:46.008
We'll fix you.

228
00:32:46.049 --> 00:32:47.718
That's all they really want.

229
00:32:47.759 --> 00:32:49.595
We'll get them off our backs.

230
00:32:49.636 --> 00:32:50.762
Yes.

231
00:32:57.186 --> 00:33:00.480
Things are hard.

232
00:33:00.522 --> 00:33:02.733
We need to be careful.

233
00:33:05.194 --> 00:33:07.696
We need to slow down.

234
00:33:15.495 --> 00:33:20.501
You...

235
00:33:20.542 --> 00:33:21.919
need me.

236
00:34:12.010 --> 00:34:15.013
[gravel crunching]

237
00:34:59.057 --> 00:35:05.063
[jaunty piano music playing]

238
00:35:32.883 --> 00:35:34.218
[music stops]

239
00:35:52.611 --> 00:35:54.112
- Hello?

240
00:35:58.617 --> 00:36:00.160
Did you put this here?

241
00:36:18.971 --> 00:36:21.098
[sighs]

242
00:36:43.078 --> 00:36:44.413
Why?

243
00:37:09.229 --> 00:37:10.522
You can see me?

244
00:37:32.127 --> 00:37:36.548
And you...understand me?

245
00:37:55.692 --> 00:37:57.986
Where did all these things
come from?

246
00:38:12.543 --> 00:38:14.044
[object clatters]

247
00:38:25.305 --> 00:38:27.516
[wood creaking]

248
00:38:41.905 --> 00:38:44.908
[phone line ringing]

249
00:39:14.062 --> 00:39:15.606
- You've reached
George House Hospice.

250
00:39:15.647 --> 00:39:16.857
We're either busy
at the moment.

251
00:39:16.899 --> 00:39:18.275
or you've reached us
after hours.

252
00:39:18.317 --> 00:39:19.401
Leave your name and number.

253
00:39:19.443 --> 00:39:21.153
and someone
will get back to you shortly.

254
00:39:21.195 --> 00:39:22.529
[phone line beeps]

255
00:39:22.571 --> 00:39:25.741
- Hi. my name's
Caroline Dalgarno.

256
00:39:25.782 --> 00:39:28.035
I am calling to see if you
have someone in care there.

257
00:39:28.076 --> 00:39:30.412
His name is Peter Dalgarno.

258
00:39:30.454 --> 00:39:32.289
If you wouldn't mind.
give me a ring back.

259
00:39:32.331 --> 00:39:38.170
My number is 077-009-00136.

260
00:39:38.212 --> 00:39:39.671
OK. thank you very much.

261
00:39:39.713 --> 00:39:41.465
Bye-bye.

262
00:39:41.507 --> 00:39:42.466
[phone line beeps]

263
00:39:42.508 --> 00:39:44.760
[clears throat. sighs]

264
00:40:23.757 --> 00:40:25.133
Yes.

265
00:40:30.222 --> 00:40:32.057
I was--

266
00:40:34.184 --> 00:40:37.980
I was moving home. actually.

267
00:40:40.023 --> 00:40:45.362
My--my landlord
wanted to renovate.

268
00:40:45.404 --> 00:40:48.448
and there was nowhere else
I could afford. so...

269
00:40:56.957 --> 00:40:59.334
I was hiding everything
by the train station.

270
00:40:59.376 --> 00:41:01.587
I didn't have
anywhere else to put it.

271
00:41:03.839 --> 00:41:05.132
Is that OK?

272
00:41:15.392 --> 00:41:20.230
But I'll leave...soon.

273
00:41:23.567 --> 00:41:28.030
Is he--is he coming back?

274
00:41:36.496 --> 00:41:39.708
Plants...

275
00:41:39.750 --> 00:41:42.794
and clothes

276
00:41:42.836 --> 00:41:47.299
and drawings and some books.

277
00:41:54.723 --> 00:41:56.141
I'm not very good.

278
00:41:59.853 --> 00:42:03.357
I should be better
at perspective.

279
00:42:03.398 --> 00:42:05.817
making things
look three-dimensional.

280
00:42:38.892 --> 00:42:40.102
That's you.

281
00:42:42.688 --> 00:42:44.273
You can just see a little bit.

282
00:42:44.314 --> 00:42:49.236
It's a photograph
taken from the road.

283
00:42:49.278 --> 00:42:50.696
That's your roof.

284
00:42:54.074 --> 00:42:55.325
Yeah. exactly.

285
00:42:55.367 --> 00:42:58.954
They--they take
all these photographs

286
00:42:58.996 --> 00:43:02.624
and put them together
so it feels like

287
00:43:02.666 --> 00:43:04.168
you're walking down the street.

288
00:43:04.209 --> 00:43:06.545
You can go anywhere.

289
00:43:12.467 --> 00:43:17.222
Sometimes when I was at uni.
I would put in my home address

290
00:43:17.264 --> 00:43:19.725
and pretend I was walking
along my road.

291
00:43:23.437 --> 00:43:27.065
It's just a few miles
that way. actually.

292
00:43:30.694 --> 00:43:32.487
I used to come
past here all the time.

293
00:43:32.529 --> 00:43:36.074
but I never came
down this road.

294
00:43:36.116 --> 00:43:37.868
I never knew about you.

295
00:43:54.426 --> 00:43:58.180
[singing]
Familiar places

296
00:43:58.222 --> 00:44:01.850
Familiar people

297
00:44:01.892 --> 00:44:05.229
Always the same
bright sunny day

298
00:44:08.106 --> 00:44:09.983
It's like being a kid again.

299
00:44:23.080 --> 00:44:24.873
We're not--

300
00:44:28.585 --> 00:44:30.462
We're not--

301
00:44:34.758 --> 00:44:35.968
I knew he was ill.

302
00:44:41.390 --> 00:44:42.975
He can be distant.

303
00:45:12.296 --> 00:45:15.299
[phone buzzing]

304
00:45:20.929 --> 00:45:22.639
- Hello. Caroline?

305
00:45:24.308 --> 00:45:26.101
Caroline?
- Yes. hi.

306
00:45:26.143 --> 00:45:27.186
- Oh. hi.

307
00:45:27.227 --> 00:45:30.397
[laughs] Yes.

308
00:45:30.439 --> 00:45:32.900
You all right?

309
00:45:32.941 --> 00:45:33.942
- How are you doing?

310
00:45:33.984 --> 00:45:35.319
- Oh. I'm all right.

311
00:45:35.360 --> 00:45:36.486
Yeah.

312
00:45:36.528 --> 00:45:37.571
I'm all right.

313
00:45:37.613 --> 00:45:41.867
You know. they're--how's uni?

314
00:45:41.909 --> 00:45:43.493
- Yeah. fine. Good.

315
00:45:43.535 --> 00:45:47.623
- Making your wee drawings.
yeah. your wee houses.

316
00:45:47.664 --> 00:45:51.210
I still have that one
from your application.

317
00:45:51.251 --> 00:45:53.754
your portfolio. the--

318
00:45:56.256 --> 00:45:57.925
You keeping safe over there?

319
00:45:57.966 --> 00:46:00.886
- Yeah. of course.

320
00:46:00.928 --> 00:46:05.140
Yeah. everything's fine.

321
00:46:05.182 --> 00:46:07.142
How are you doing?

322
00:46:07.184 --> 00:46:08.977
- I'm all right.

323
00:46:09.019 --> 00:46:12.105
[chuckles] Yeah. I do worry.

324
00:46:14.191 --> 00:46:17.528
I put it out of my head.
of course. but--

325
00:46:23.325 --> 00:46:26.078
I go on my walks.
and I imagine

326
00:46:26.119 --> 00:46:29.706
what you must be getting up to.

327
00:46:29.748 --> 00:46:32.835
going around. living your life.

328
00:46:36.338 --> 00:46:37.965
Did I ever tell you that?

329
00:46:44.930 --> 00:46:47.432
- Dad?

330
00:46:47.474 --> 00:46:50.394
- Sorry. sorry. just had
a wee moment there.

331
00:46:50.435 --> 00:46:52.604
[laughs]

332
00:46:52.646 --> 00:46:54.189
So how are you?
How is uni?

333
00:46:54.231 --> 00:46:55.858
- Yeah. it's fine.

334
00:46:55.899 --> 00:46:57.818
- [laughs]

335
00:46:57.860 --> 00:46:58.861
- It's hard.

336
00:46:58.902 --> 00:47:00.070
- Oh. I know.

337
00:47:00.112 --> 00:47:02.114
You don't have to tell me.

338
00:47:02.155 --> 00:47:03.282
I had an awful time.

339
00:47:03.323 --> 00:47:05.200
I didn't even make it
through a full year.

340
00:47:05.242 --> 00:47:07.327
- I know.
- [laughs]

341
00:47:09.454 --> 00:47:13.750
Remember when we lived
in Auchenblae.

342
00:47:13.792 --> 00:47:14.877
the nice house?

343
00:47:14.918 --> 00:47:16.378
Yeah.

344
00:47:16.420 --> 00:47:18.881
Oh. no. no. that was
before you were born.

345
00:47:18.922 --> 00:47:21.633
[chuckles]
No. Cat was pregnant.

346
00:47:21.675 --> 00:47:23.760
Of course
you wouldn't remember.

347
00:47:27.514 --> 00:47:30.475
That was the best time.
Caroline.

348
00:47:30.517 --> 00:47:36.523
Seeing you on the ultrasound.
so cozy. so safe inside. yeah.

349
00:47:39.234 --> 00:47:40.777
I thought about
that picture of you.

350
00:47:40.819 --> 00:47:46.158
and I wished
you could stay in there

351
00:47:46.200 --> 00:47:51.205
and not go out into the awful.
dangerous world.

352
00:47:59.671 --> 00:48:01.131
Oh.

353
00:48:01.173 --> 00:48:02.257
Oh. dear. oh. dear.

354
00:48:02.299 --> 00:48:03.300
There I go again.

355
00:48:03.342 --> 00:48:06.053
I'm sorry. love.

356
00:48:06.094 --> 00:48:07.262
It's the drugs.

357
00:48:07.304 --> 00:48:08.805
The good shit.

358
00:48:08.847 --> 00:48:11.934
Let me know. and I'll see
if I can hook you up with some.

359
00:48:11.975 --> 00:48:13.602
- I'm gonna come
and see you. Dad.

360
00:48:13.644 --> 00:48:15.354
- Oh. no. no. No. no.

361
00:48:15.395 --> 00:48:16.522
- Yes.

362
00:48:16.563 --> 00:48:17.940
Yeah.

363
00:48:19.608 --> 00:48:22.569
What did they do with all
your composition books?

364
00:48:22.611 --> 00:48:23.820
- No. don't do that.

365
00:48:23.862 --> 00:48:25.572
- No. it's all right.

366
00:48:25.614 --> 00:48:27.366
It's OK.

367
00:48:27.407 --> 00:48:29.076
Where are you?

368
00:48:29.117 --> 00:48:31.161
- No. focus on school.
Caroline.

369
00:48:31.203 --> 00:48:33.247
- Where are you. Dad?

370
00:48:33.288 --> 00:48:35.624
- Oh. I'm just at home.

371
00:48:42.589 --> 00:48:44.007
- You're at home?

372
00:48:44.049 --> 00:48:47.052
- Yeah. I'm sat in the kitchen.
looking out the window.

373
00:48:47.094 --> 00:48:49.638
I've got your little
clay sculpture

374
00:48:49.680 --> 00:48:53.058
here on the windowsill.

375
00:48:53.100 --> 00:48:55.310
Some robins in the bird feeder.

376
00:48:58.564 --> 00:49:00.065
- How many robins?

377
00:49:02.401 --> 00:49:04.903
- Three of them.

378
00:49:04.945 --> 00:49:08.240
- Is it nice there?

379
00:49:08.282 --> 00:49:09.783
- It's beautiful.

380
00:49:13.412 --> 00:49:15.163
Oh. I'm sorry.

381
00:49:15.205 --> 00:49:17.040
I have to go.
Liam at the door.

382
00:49:17.082 --> 00:49:19.543
- OK.
OK. well. I'll see you soon.

383
00:49:19.585 --> 00:49:21.712
- See you soon.

384
00:49:21.753 --> 00:49:23.046
[phone line beeps]

385
00:49:31.180 --> 00:49:33.557
- [sniffles. sighs]

386
00:50:09.801 --> 00:50:11.345
[exhales sharply]

387
00:50:18.727 --> 00:50:20.312
You fixed the window.

388
00:50:56.515 --> 00:50:59.518
[birds singing]

389
00:52:53.465 --> 00:52:54.842
When was that?

390
00:53:08.355 --> 00:53:11.775
Do you remember
a time before that?

391
00:53:21.785 --> 00:53:24.830
You fixed the window.

392
00:53:24.872 --> 00:53:26.331
You can fix yourself.

393
00:53:37.301 --> 00:53:38.760
What do you eat?

394
00:53:44.933 --> 00:53:46.476
Do you know what you are?

395
00:53:50.439 --> 00:53:52.399
Do you know how long
you've been here?

396
00:54:04.661 --> 00:54:10.417
Does--does anyone else
know about you?

397
00:54:21.136 --> 00:54:22.846
What happens to things?

398
00:54:25.599 --> 00:54:29.478
You take them away
and you bring them back.

399
00:54:34.983 --> 00:54:36.401
Where does it go?

400
00:55:17.985 --> 00:55:20.988
[doorknob rattling]

401
00:55:53.520 --> 00:55:58.025
I don't have any money.
but I could walk to him.

402
00:56:01.236 --> 00:56:02.446
It's four hours.

403
00:56:05.908 --> 00:56:07.034
I can do that.

404
00:56:38.815 --> 00:56:40.776
I don't need any of this.

405
00:56:54.414 --> 00:56:57.417
[birds singing]

406
00:57:15.394 --> 00:57:16.478
[soft metallic clank]

407
00:57:35.372 --> 00:57:38.375
[phone buzzing]

408
00:58:07.988 --> 00:58:09.239
This is you.

409
00:58:12.367 --> 00:58:13.744
A slate roof.

410
00:58:15.954 --> 00:58:18.081
Slate ridge tiles.

411
00:58:19.750 --> 00:58:24.338
A lead verge gutter.

412
00:58:24.379 --> 00:58:27.925
Bay window and a French door

413
00:58:27.966 --> 00:58:30.177
up on the gable end.

414
00:58:35.891 --> 00:58:38.936
Top upper windows
with recessed window reveals.

415
00:58:38.977 --> 00:58:40.103
Scottish style.

416
00:58:40.145 --> 00:58:43.106
set back in the cavity
to keep out some of the rain.

417
00:58:46.235 --> 00:58:49.488
In good shape. all in all.

418
00:58:49.530 --> 00:58:51.198
[chuckles]

419
00:58:52.824 --> 00:58:56.245
See how I put lines in
for perspective?

420
00:59:01.250 --> 00:59:06.046
This is the vanishing point...

421
00:59:06.088 --> 00:59:11.176
where it all comes together
and ends.

422
00:59:18.100 --> 00:59:21.770
To the house without an occupant
from the girl without a home.

423
00:59:26.358 --> 00:59:27.860
Thank you.

424
00:59:48.964 --> 00:59:51.216
[door creaks]

425
01:00:42.976 --> 01:00:45.979
[rain pattering]

426
01:01:28.897 --> 01:01:31.149
[thunder rumbling]

427
01:01:35.487 --> 01:01:38.490
[birds singing]

428
01:02:02.222 --> 01:02:04.850
[gravel crunching]

429
01:02:04.892 --> 01:02:07.144
- Just go and open the door.

430
01:02:07.186 --> 01:02:09.646
- Here we go.

431
01:02:09.688 --> 01:02:12.691
[lock clicks. door creaks]

432
01:02:28.832 --> 01:02:30.584
- Want to have a look in here?

433
01:02:33.337 --> 01:02:34.838
Come on. let's have a look.

434
01:02:45.974 --> 01:02:47.434
Wow.

435
01:02:49.811 --> 01:02:52.439
So big.
[gasps]

436
01:02:52.481 --> 01:02:54.650
Can we see
what's out the window?

437
01:02:54.691 --> 01:02:56.401
[baby fussing]

438
01:02:56.443 --> 01:02:58.570
Oh. it's OK.

439
01:02:58.612 --> 01:03:00.364
OK.

440
01:03:00.405 --> 01:03:01.448
It's OK.

441
01:03:01.490 --> 01:03:02.741
Look at the flowers.

442
01:03:02.783 --> 01:03:05.285
[gasps] Wow.

443
01:03:05.327 --> 01:03:07.621
Look at the flowers.

444
01:03:07.663 --> 01:03:08.914
So pretty.

445
01:03:10.082 --> 01:03:11.583
So pretty.

446
01:03:19.091 --> 01:03:21.718
[speaking indistinctly]

447
01:03:23.470 --> 01:03:24.471
Hon?

448
01:03:27.391 --> 01:03:28.767
Can we get a picture?

449
01:03:31.687 --> 01:03:33.647
You OK? Oh.

450
01:03:33.689 --> 01:03:35.357
[baby fusses]

451
01:03:46.743 --> 01:03:48.579
[baby fussing]

452
01:03:48.620 --> 01:03:49.788
You're OK.

453
01:03:55.627 --> 01:03:59.381
Hon. you got my phone?

454
01:03:59.423 --> 01:04:01.758
- Huh?
- You got my phone?

455
01:04:01.800 --> 01:04:05.137
- I don't have it.

456
01:04:05.179 --> 01:04:07.097
- Thank you.

457
01:04:07.139 --> 01:04:09.474
Oh. should we go back?

458
01:04:09.516 --> 01:04:10.893
[gasps]

459
01:04:10.934 --> 01:04:12.227
Can you take it?

460
01:04:12.269 --> 01:04:13.604
- Yeah.

461
01:04:15.105 --> 01:04:16.481
Let's go.

462
01:04:16.523 --> 01:04:17.649
- Go on.
Say cheese.

463
01:04:17.691 --> 01:04:20.194
- Cheese!

464
01:04:20.235 --> 01:04:21.236
[camera shutter snaps]

465
01:04:22.112 --> 01:04:25.908
- Go on. give us a smile. then.

466
01:04:25.949 --> 01:04:28.327
Aw. he's a grump now.

467
01:04:28.368 --> 01:04:30.495
- [sighs. speaks indistinctly]

468
01:04:36.877 --> 01:04:38.086
[baby fusses]

469
01:04:38.128 --> 01:04:41.048
Yeah. I know.
I know. I know.

470
01:04:41.089 --> 01:04:42.466
I know.

471
01:04:47.429 --> 01:04:50.432
[indistinct chatter]

472
01:05:28.262 --> 01:05:31.265
[car engine rumbling]

473
01:05:31.306 --> 01:05:34.309
[rain pattering]

474
01:05:36.895 --> 01:05:38.313
[car door slams]

475
01:05:48.740 --> 01:05:50.784
- Hiya.
- Hi. Are you--

476
01:05:50.826 --> 01:05:52.703
- I'm an officer of the court.

477
01:05:52.744 --> 01:05:54.955
You're the owner
of this property.

478
01:05:54.997 --> 01:05:56.999
- I am the estate agent.

479
01:05:57.040 --> 01:05:59.418
- No. you're the owner.
the inheritor.

480
01:05:59.459 --> 01:06:01.378
You're Duncan Patterson.

481
01:06:01.420 --> 01:06:03.422
I've come about the CPO.

482
01:06:03.463 --> 01:06:05.424
You wrote to the minister
and the council

483
01:06:05.465 --> 01:06:07.426
objecting to the CPO. yeah?

484
01:06:07.467 --> 01:06:09.428
- Said I have 21 days.

485
01:06:09.469 --> 01:06:10.596
- That's right.

486
01:06:10.637 --> 01:06:12.931
You objected to the CPO.

487
01:06:12.973 --> 01:06:15.934
You said you had
fixed the property up...

488
01:06:15.976 --> 01:06:16.977
- That's right.

489
01:06:17.019 --> 01:06:18.353
- And you had
an interested buyer.

490
01:06:18.395 --> 01:06:19.479
- That's right.

491
01:06:19.521 --> 01:06:21.398
- If you do actually
have a buyer.

492
01:06:21.440 --> 01:06:23.609
then that's something
the court needs to know.

493
01:06:23.650 --> 01:06:25.485
That's good news.

494
01:06:25.527 --> 01:06:26.987
- Yes.

495
01:06:28.655 --> 01:06:29.740
- Who is it?

496
01:06:29.781 --> 01:06:32.868
Who's the solicitor
they're working with?

497
01:06:32.910 --> 01:06:35.037
- I need to send it to you
in writing.

498
01:06:35.078 --> 01:06:37.289
- We've sent numerous notices.

499
01:06:37.331 --> 01:06:40.542
I myself have been here several
times trying to track you down.

500
01:06:40.584 --> 01:06:41.752
but you're nowhere to be found.

501
01:06:41.793 --> 01:06:44.505
- Well. I'm here now.
- Yes. you are.

502
01:06:44.546 --> 01:06:47.090
And I'm here to see
if what you said is true.

503
01:06:47.132 --> 01:06:48.509
And clearly. it isn't.

504
01:06:48.550 --> 01:06:49.676
- What are you gonna do with it?

505
01:06:49.718 --> 01:06:50.928
You gonna tear it down?

506
01:06:50.969 --> 01:06:52.930
[ominous rumbling]

507
01:06:52.971 --> 01:06:55.390
- It's uninhabited
and derelict.

508
01:06:55.432 --> 01:06:56.934
- It's not derelict.

509
01:06:56.975 --> 01:06:58.727
- People have reported
vandalism.

510
01:06:58.769 --> 01:07:00.521
broken windows. squatters.

511
01:07:00.562 --> 01:07:02.898
- What?
There's no--

512
01:07:02.940 --> 01:07:04.733
[rumbling continues]

513
01:07:04.775 --> 01:07:07.736
Do you see any broken windows?

514
01:07:07.778 --> 01:07:08.946
- Not currently.

515
01:07:08.987 --> 01:07:09.988
- Or squatters?

516
01:07:10.030 --> 01:07:11.615
- Houses like this
are sitting empty

517
01:07:11.657 --> 01:07:14.493
while people are desperately
needing somewhere to live.

518
01:07:14.535 --> 01:07:17.204
The waiting list
for council housing is full.

519
01:07:17.246 --> 01:07:18.956
- Not here.

520
01:07:18.997 --> 01:07:20.123
Nobody wants to live here.

521
01:07:20.165 --> 01:07:23.210
They want to visit.
They don't want to live here.

522
01:07:23.252 --> 01:07:25.587
- If I'm not able to go--

523
01:07:25.629 --> 01:07:27.548
- Go inside and have a look.

524
01:07:27.589 --> 01:07:29.675
- I'm not here for that.
- Go inside and have a look.

525
01:07:29.716 --> 01:07:31.468
There's nothing wrong with it.
- No.

526
01:07:31.510 --> 01:07:33.428
- Go inside yourself.

527
01:07:33.470 --> 01:07:34.680
[dull thudding]

528
01:07:34.721 --> 01:07:36.390
- Sir.

529
01:07:36.431 --> 01:07:39.142
[panting]

530
01:07:39.184 --> 01:07:41.645
Do not touch me.

531
01:08:07.546 --> 01:08:09.840
- I told you to--

532
01:08:35.616 --> 01:08:37.117
[metallic clatter]

533
01:09:54.069 --> 01:09:57.447
[footsteps tapping]

534
01:09:57.489 --> 01:10:00.492
- [breathing heavily]

535
01:10:03.537 --> 01:10:06.206
[door creaks]

536
01:10:06.248 --> 01:10:08.876
I--I'm so sorry.

537
01:10:08.917 --> 01:10:10.586
No. I'm really sorry.

538
01:10:10.627 --> 01:10:14.631
I just need to get
my--my phone.

539
01:10:29.104 --> 01:10:31.815
- Hiya.
- [gasps]

540
01:10:31.857 --> 01:10:33.692
[breathing heavily]

541
01:10:33.734 --> 01:10:35.485
- It's all right.

542
01:10:35.527 --> 01:10:37.988
I just want to talk to you.

543
01:10:38.030 --> 01:10:39.406
Come outside. please.

544
01:10:45.454 --> 01:10:48.790
What have you been
doing in there?

545
01:10:48.832 --> 01:10:52.544
- Oh. no. I haven't--

546
01:10:54.046 --> 01:10:56.590
I just saw
the door was open.

547
01:10:56.632 --> 01:10:58.842
I'm sorry.
[laughs nervously]

548
01:10:58.884 --> 01:11:00.594
- It's all right.

549
01:11:00.636 --> 01:11:02.930
Well. come out now.

550
01:11:10.354 --> 01:11:14.107
You've been staying in here.
haven't you?

551
01:11:14.149 --> 01:11:16.902
I'm the owner.

552
01:11:16.944 --> 01:11:18.195
But that's all right.

553
01:11:21.114 --> 01:11:23.242
- I need my phone.

554
01:11:23.283 --> 01:11:24.660
- Your phone?
- Yeah.

555
01:11:24.701 --> 01:11:29.581
I just--I just need to get
my phone. and then I'll go.

556
01:11:29.623 --> 01:11:31.917
- You can use my phone.
What do you need?

557
01:11:31.959 --> 01:11:34.837
Do you need a lift?
- No. no.

558
01:11:34.878 --> 01:11:37.339
- I've got money.

559
01:11:37.381 --> 01:11:39.633
It's all right.
- [laughs]

560
01:11:39.675 --> 01:11:42.052
- I just want to help.

561
01:11:42.094 --> 01:11:46.014
I can help you get
whatever you want.

562
01:11:55.691 --> 01:11:57.359
[growls]

563
01:11:57.401 --> 01:12:00.696
- [panting]

564
01:12:00.737 --> 01:12:03.156
[grunts]

565
01:12:03.198 --> 01:12:06.618
[static crackling]

566
01:12:06.660 --> 01:12:09.663
[panting]

567
01:12:11.456 --> 01:12:14.459
[ominous rumbling]

568
01:12:17.379 --> 01:12:18.964
- [grunts]
- OK.

569
01:12:19.006 --> 01:12:21.508
- [groans] Stop! Stop!

570
01:12:23.177 --> 01:12:24.845
Be quiet!

571
01:12:24.887 --> 01:12:27.890
[both grunting]

572
01:12:29.600 --> 01:12:32.603
[static crackling]

573
01:12:50.829 --> 01:12:53.832
- [whimpering]

574
01:13:23.362 --> 01:13:26.490
[both panting]

575
01:13:26.532 --> 01:13:29.535
[rumbling fades]

576
01:13:36.208 --> 01:13:38.293
- [mumbling]

577
01:13:44.424 --> 01:13:46.343
Don't listen.

578
01:13:46.385 --> 01:13:48.887
Please.

579
01:13:48.929 --> 01:13:51.682
Don't listen to it.

580
01:13:51.723 --> 01:13:53.392
Please.

581
01:13:53.433 --> 01:13:55.894
- [whimpers]

582
01:13:55.936 --> 01:13:58.939
[static crackling]

583
01:14:00.732 --> 01:14:03.026
What more could I have done?

584
01:14:07.281 --> 01:14:08.824
Please.

585
01:14:10.617 --> 01:14:12.160
Please.

586
01:14:14.162 --> 01:14:16.540
Please!

587
01:14:23.505 --> 01:14:26.216
- [breathing heavily]

588
01:15:38.622 --> 01:15:40.123
- Hello. love.

589
01:15:43.252 --> 01:15:45.712
Sorry to call you again
like this.

590
01:15:45.754 --> 01:15:49.800
It's just. well...

591
01:15:49.842 --> 01:15:52.678
there are a lot of things.
a lot of things

592
01:15:52.719 --> 01:15:55.514
I thought I wanted to say.

593
01:15:57.224 --> 01:16:02.855
When I finally heard your voice.
oh. it was so nice.

594
01:16:05.190 --> 01:16:07.442
I couldn't think
of how to say it.

595
01:16:07.484 --> 01:16:09.903
[chuckles]

596
01:16:14.408 --> 01:16:16.326
I was afraid. I was.

597
01:16:16.368 --> 01:16:18.287
I was.

598
01:16:18.328 --> 01:16:19.955
Ever since you were born.

599
01:16:19.997 --> 01:16:21.790
And it made me--

600
01:16:27.045 --> 01:16:30.966
My own father. you know.
he wasn't a very good father.

601
01:16:31.008 --> 01:16:34.303
I don't think his father
had been a very good father.

602
01:16:34.344 --> 01:16:37.890
And I tried to be different.

603
01:16:37.931 --> 01:16:42.936
I chose coldness. distance.

604
01:16:42.978 --> 01:16:45.772
And I think--

605
01:16:45.814 --> 01:16:47.816
I think that was wrong too.

606
01:16:53.780 --> 01:16:57.743
I think about you
living your life.

607
01:16:57.784 --> 01:17:01.371
and it's like
being young again.

608
01:17:01.413 --> 01:17:03.040
It's like being born again.

609
01:17:05.667 --> 01:17:09.505
And I'm not afraid now.

610
01:17:09.546 --> 01:17:11.298
Not at all.

611
01:17:20.724 --> 01:17:22.476
I'm not in here.

612
01:17:24.895 --> 01:17:29.900
I'm out there.
out there living.

613
01:17:34.905 --> 01:17:37.616
You're me. aren't you?

614
01:17:48.418 --> 01:17:51.505
Oh. I'm telling you.
Caroline. these drugs. oof.

615
01:17:51.547 --> 01:17:53.173
they're something else.

616
01:17:57.302 --> 01:17:58.971
I've been feeling
a little poorly.

617
01:17:59.012 --> 01:18:03.141
I've been--
well. the nice people here.

618
01:18:03.183 --> 01:18:05.519
the nice people
who have been helping me.

619
01:18:05.561 --> 01:18:11.024
they think I could stop
all the medication.

620
01:18:11.066 --> 01:18:14.570
the pills.

621
01:18:14.611 --> 01:18:19.783
just sort of...rest.

622
01:18:21.994 --> 01:18:23.787
Sedation is what it--

623
01:18:23.829 --> 01:18:26.123
palliative sedation.

624
01:18:28.375 --> 01:18:31.128
I've been thinking about it.
but I wanted to.

625
01:18:31.170 --> 01:18:35.215
you know.
just one last time. well--

626
01:18:35.257 --> 01:18:41.180
yeah. so I might not
be able to speak again.

627
01:18:45.767 --> 01:18:48.770
[chuckles]

628
01:18:50.564 --> 01:18:52.149
Oh. dear. oh. dear.

629
01:18:59.573 --> 01:19:01.617
I wish I'd been closer to you.

630
01:19:06.371 --> 01:19:07.998
Just a silly man.

631
01:19:10.375 --> 01:19:13.754
- [sobs]

632
01:19:13.795 --> 01:19:15.839
- You'll figure it out.
won't you?

633
01:19:24.598 --> 01:19:25.807
[chuckles]

634
01:19:25.849 --> 01:19:28.018
So lovely to hear
your voice earlier.

635
01:19:28.060 --> 01:19:29.645
Hope all's well.

636
01:19:29.686 --> 01:19:30.687
[line beeps]

637
01:19:56.880 --> 01:20:01.510
- A vanishing point...

638
01:20:01.552 --> 01:20:06.682
where it all
comes together...

639
01:20:06.723 --> 01:20:08.517
and ends.

640
01:20:24.992 --> 01:20:30.330
Where do people go
when they disappear?

641
01:20:44.094 --> 01:20:45.470
I could stay.

642
01:20:51.393 --> 01:20:53.437
I have nowhere else.

643
01:20:56.231 --> 01:20:58.192
No one will miss me.

644
01:21:01.862 --> 01:21:03.322
Let me stay.

645
01:21:10.662 --> 01:21:12.414
Let me go inside.

646
01:21:17.336 --> 01:21:18.754
Please.

647
01:21:47.533 --> 01:21:49.076
[sighs]

648
01:22:00.379 --> 01:22:03.340
[door clicks open. creaks]

649
01:22:13.642 --> 01:22:16.645
[footsteps tapping]

650
01:22:48.302 --> 01:22:49.928
[door creaks]

651
01:23:26.340 --> 01:23:32.346
[playful music]

652
01:24:34.199 --> 01:24:40.205
[somber music]

653
01:25:43.101 --> 01:25:46.104
[train rumbling softly]

654
01:25:58.033 --> 01:26:02.079
- This is the 5:02 service
to Edinburgh Waverley.

655
01:26:02.120 --> 01:26:05.415
Calling at Carnoustie. Dundee...

656
01:26:05.457 --> 01:26:07.125
- Tickets. please.

657
01:26:07.167 --> 01:26:12.673
- Cupar. Haymarket.
and Edinburgh Waverley.

658
01:26:12.714 --> 01:26:14.508
- Wee project. eh?

659
01:26:14.550 --> 01:26:15.634
- Yeah.

660
01:26:15.676 --> 01:26:17.052
I am an architect student.

661
01:26:17.094 --> 01:26:18.637
- All right.

662
01:26:18.679 --> 01:26:19.930
Tickets. please.

663
01:26:28.272 --> 01:26:31.066
- He's right.

664
01:26:31.108 --> 01:26:33.193
I do this thing with my eyebrows
when I know I need

665
01:26:33.235 --> 01:26:35.737
to acknowledge
what someone's saying

666
01:26:35.779 --> 01:26:38.156
but I don't want to engage

667
01:26:38.198 --> 01:26:40.075
and I have nothing to say.

668
01:26:43.287 --> 01:26:44.580
Just like him.

669
01:26:51.086 --> 01:26:53.088
All these little
bits of our lives

670
01:26:53.130 --> 01:26:55.591
through the darkness
of history.

671
01:26:58.802 --> 01:27:04.057
We're repositories of millions
of lives and stories

672
01:27:04.099 --> 01:27:06.393
reconstructed
into something that thinks

673
01:27:06.435 --> 01:27:08.228
it's new and unique.

674
01:27:12.816 --> 01:27:14.484
And maybe that's it.

675
01:27:17.529 --> 01:27:18.822
Maybe that's all.

676
01:27:24.703 --> 01:27:26.997
An old ghost in a new house.

677
01:28:01.865 --> 01:28:03.075
That's him.

678
01:28:20.342 --> 01:28:22.010
Are you comfortable?

679
01:29:12.728 --> 01:29:18.734
[tranquil piano music]

679
01:29:19.305 --> 01:30:19.636
Tired of searching for subtitles?
Ray generates them instantly: getray.app
